    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0104" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg97"/>

                <head>No. 58.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just received a cable message from
                    Capt. J. C. Watson, commander of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">San
                        Francisco</hi>, at Colon, a copy of which is found on another page of this
                    dispatch. I also herewith confirm the sending of the reply found attached to the
                    above.</p>
                <pb facs="0105" n="98" xml:id="pg98"/>
                <p>I am still in the dark as to the Department instructions referred to, and must
                    necessarily remain so for some days. The instructions of the 24th of May will be
                    due here on the 16th of June. After their receipt I will have no means of
                    reaching Captain Watson.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d58-a1.xml" xpointer="d58-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d58-a2.xml" xpointer="d58-a2"/>
